---
import Button from './Button.astro';
---

<section id="why" class="section story">
  <div class="container story-grid">
    <div class="story-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why this exists</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">
        It's a commonly known fact that
        <br />
        <span class="hl-teal">rolling release updates can ruin everything.</span>
      </h2>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          You have probably experienced a routine update take down your graphics
          driver, or your audio pipeline, or the one app your big hobby uses. Then
          you spent a whole day putting it back together.
        </p>
        <p>It's not your fault.</p>
        <p>
          <strong>
            Most Linux distrobutions are mutable systems that are patched in place,
            and that method makes every update unpridictable. There is no before or backup
            to go back to, unless you manually set it up.
          </strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          Atomic images are safer: The root filesystem is read-only, versioned, and has
          no in-between state. Updates write new snapshots, and you just reboot into it.
          If anything goes wrong, you just select the old entry from the bootloader with just
          a few keypresses at boot, and you're back in action.
          An update writes a new snapshot alongside the old one, reboots into it, and if
        </p>
        <p>
          The Thallium Suite is a collection of unique atomic distros: a catalogue of images
          usable with bootc, a system that lets you boot from said containers with
          reproducible layers and easy atomic rollbacks.
          boring.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="story-actions">
        <Button href="#faq" variant="teal">
          How it works
        </Button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="story-aside" aria-label="The difference in one line">
      <div class="compare">
        <div class="compare-pane compare-old">
          <h3 class="compare-title">Classic distro</h3>
          <ul class="compare-list">
            <li>
              <span class="x">✕</span> In between updates
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="x">✕</span> Broken states
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="x">✕</span> Recovery means reinstall or 5 hours
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="x">✕</span> "Works on my machine"
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="compare-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
          →
        </div>

        <div class="compare-pane compare-new">
          <h3 class="compare-title">Atomic image</h3>
          <ul class="compare-list">
            <li>
              <span class="tick">✓</span> Snapshots rebooted into and out of
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tick">✓</span> Previous deployment kept safe
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tick">✓</span> Roll back at boot easily
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tick">✓</span> Pinned and signed digests
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="story-aside-note">
        Same hardware and kernel, but a completely different failure model.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .story {
    background: var(--ink-raised);
    border-block: 2px solid var(--ink-line);
  }

  .story-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .story-copy {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    justify-items: start;
  }

  .hl-teal {
    color: var(--teal);
  }

  .story-actions {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  /* --- compare card -------------------------------------------------------- */

  .story-aside {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 1.75rem);
    background: var(--ink);
    border: 3px solid var(--paper);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-paper-md);
  }

  .compare {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .compare-pane {
    padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 2px solid var(--ink-line);
  }

  .compare-old {
    background: #1a1520;
    border-color: #3a2b33;
  }

  .compare-new {
    background: #0f2a26;
    border-color: #1d4a42;
  }

  .compare-title {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .compare-old .compare-title {
    color: var(--coral);
  }
  .compare-new .compare-title {
    color: var(--teal);
  }

  .compare-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .x {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--coral);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .tick {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--green);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .compare-arrow {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .story-aside-note {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-align: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .story-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr;
    }

    .story-aside {
      position: sticky;
      top: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
